Logic :

create a arr which is of size 3 for storing the recently visited index of each character
iterate each character in for loop
store the character to its corresponding index (recently visited) in array
check whether the substring contains all the character , i.e., check whether all the 3 values in array are greater than -1
if yes , then
add the ans with the least visited character i.e., the minimum value of the three
finally , return the answer


Intuition :

find the minimum substring which has all three characters 
and subtract it with the least visited character to get all the possible substrings


Code :

class Solution {
    public int numberOfSubstrings(String s) {
        int[] arr=new int[3];
        int ans=0;
        Arrays.fill(arr,-1);
        for(int i=0;i<s.length();i++){
            char ch=s.charAt(i);
            arr[ch-97]=i;
            if(arr[0]!=-1 && arr[1]!=-1 && arr[2]!=-1){
                ans=ans+(1+Math.min(arr[0],Math.min(arr[1],arr[2])));
            }
        }
        return ans;
    }
}
